group index
note Where syntax colours come from and where they are painted. tree-sitter does the colouring for every language regardless of which backend supplied the symbols: the grammar's own highlight query runs once per file during the parse, and its captures are bucketed into per-line byte spans with a small class byte. The spans are cached with the rest of the file, so nothing re-parses to draw. The second half of the path is the drawing side, shared by the path document, the Source view and the graph nodes.

